good-natured man.

490
00:24:21,390 --> 00:24:24,014
- Now bingo is his name-o.
- Look at him now.

491
00:24:24,014 --> 00:24:25,947
He looks just like one
of the flying monkeys

492
00:24:25,947 --> 00:24:28,743
from "the wizard of oz."

493
00:24:32,850 --> 00:24:35,957
Now he'’s his own
best friend.

494
00:24:35,957 --> 00:24:37,924
[Growling, muttering]

495
00:24:37,924 --> 00:24:39,961
[Growling]

496
00:24:39,961 --> 00:24:43,171
He'’s no longer human.
He'’s a wolf.

497
00:24:43,171 --> 00:24:45,207
Snarling, ferocious.

498
00:24:45,207 --> 00:24:46,968
Lusting for the kill.

499
00:24:46,968 --> 00:24:48,452
He needs to go outside,
too, I think.

500
00:24:48,452 --> 00:24:54,009
This is a scientific
miracle, gentlemen.

501
00:24:54,009 --> 00:24:55,908
Hey, it'’s William s. Burroughs.

502
00:24:55,908 --> 00:24:57,323
You'’re a madman, Cameron.

503
00:24:57,323 --> 00:24:59,152
Your claim is
ridiculous.

504
00:24:59,152 --> 00:25:02,017
That'’s exactly what you said
in the newspapers,

505
00:25:02,017 --> 00:25:05,849
professor Blaine--
that I was a madman.

506
00:25:05,849 --> 00:25:07,885
I may be mad,
but you'’re transparent.

507
00:25:07,885 --> 00:25:10,854
... science chair
at the university.

508
00:25:10,854 --> 00:25:14,305
Perhaps you'’ll change
your mind one day soon,

509
00:25:14,305 --> 00:25:17,377
when Petro tears
at your throat.

510
00:25:17,377 --> 00:25:19,552
Poppycock!

511
00:25:19,552 --> 00:25:21,036
But look.

512
00:25:21,036 --> 00:25:23,522
[Petro snarling]

513
00:25:23,522 --> 00:25:25,972
I Don'’t think they should
let him get on the furniture.

514
00:25:25,972 --> 00:25:28,250
He'’s getting all
tangled up.

515
00:25:28,250 --> 00:25:31,253
Even now, he'’d like to be
at his work.

516
00:25:31,253 --> 00:25:33,186
